{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:1", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "(Objection:) If the own-nature of all things is nowhere found, your own statement is also without own-nature and cannot refute own-nature.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute"], "reported_by_opponent": true, "notes": "The objector's view (Naiyāyika/Ābhidharmika in the commentary), known through Nāgārjuna's statement of it.", "disputes": ["dsp:can-emptiness-be-asserted"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:22", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "22"}, "paraphrase": "The dependent arising of things is what is called emptiness; my words, being dependently arisen, are without own-nature, yet they function — as carts, cloth and pots, though empty, carry wood, grass and earth, and hold honey, water and milk.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:language-and-emptiness"], "disputes": ["dsp:can-emptiness-be-asserted"], "notes": "Verse with auto-commentary; exact verse division from memory.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:23", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "23"}, "paraphrase": "As a magically created man might stop another magically created man, or an illusory being one produced by another illusion, so is this negation.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute", "sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:nirmita", "trm:maya"], "concepts": ["cpt:illusion-similes", "cpt:language-and-emptiness"], "disputes": ["dsp:can-emptiness-be-asserted"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:29", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "29"}, "paraphrase": "If I had any thesis, that fault would be mine; but I have no thesis, and so no fault is mine.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute", "ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:pratijna"], "concepts": ["cpt:no-thesis"], "disputes": ["dsp:debate-without-thesis", "dsp:can-emptiness-be-asserted"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:30", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "30"}, "paraphrase": "If I apprehended anything by perception and the other means of knowledge, I would affirm or deny it; since there is no such thing, no reproach applies to me.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute"], "terms": ["trm:pramana"], "concepts": ["cpt:no-thesis"], "disputes": ["dsp:establishment-of-pramanas"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:31-33", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "31-33"}, "paraphrase": "If the means of knowledge establish their objects, what establishes the means of knowledge? If other means of knowledge, there is an infinite regress, and neither beginning, middle nor end is established; if they are established without means of knowledge, your position is abandoned.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute"], "terms": ["trm:pramana", "trm:prameya"], "concepts": ["cpt:madhyamaka-critique-of-nyaya"], "disputes": ["dsp:establishment-of-pramanas"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:34-39", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "34-39"}, "paraphrase": "(To the reply that the means of knowledge establish themselves and others as fire illumines itself and others:) fire does not illumine itself, for darkness is not seen in fire as a pot is seen in darkness; if it lit itself it would also burn itself.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute"], "disputes": ["dsp:establishment-of-pramanas"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:46-51", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "46-51"}, "paraphrase": "If the means of knowledge are established by the objects of knowledge and the objects by the means, neither is established, for what is to be established cannot establish what establishes it.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute"], "terms": ["trm:pramana", "trm:prameya"], "disputes": ["dsp:establishment-of-pramanas"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:5-6", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "5-6"}, "paraphrase": "(Objection:) If you deny things after apprehending them by perception, that very perception by which things are apprehended does not exist for you; the same holds for inference, testimony and comparison.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute"], "reported_by_opponent": true, "terms": ["trm:pramana", "trm:pratyaksa", "trm:anumana"], "disputes": ["dsp:establishment-of-pramanas"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:70", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "70"}, "paraphrase": "For whom emptiness is possible, all things are possible; for whom emptiness is not possible, nothing is possible.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "dispute"], "terms": ["trm:sunyata"], "disputes": ["dsp:madhyamaka-nihilism-charge"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:vigrahavyavartani:71", "source": "src:vigrahavyavartani", "location": {"ref": "71"}, "paraphrase": "I bow to the incomparable Buddha, who taught that emptiness, dependent origination and the middle way have one meaning.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:sunyata", "cpt:middle-way", "cpt:dependent-origination"], "notes": "Closing homage after v. 70; numbering from memory.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna", "tch:gotama-buddha"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
